Experiment: WLAN Penetration Testing using Kismet (Kali Linux)
🎯 Aim

To analyze wireless networks and identify their security configurations using Kismet in Kali Linux.

🎯 Objectives
To understand WLAN penetration testing
To scan wireless networks using Kismet
To identify SSIDs and connected devices
To analyze encryption types (WEP/WPA/WPA2)
To study wireless network behavior
🧠 Concept (Short for Viva)

WLAN penetration testing involves analyzing wireless networks to detect vulnerabilities.

Kismet is a:

Passive wireless network monitoring tool
Detects networks without sending packets
Identifies hidden SSIDs and connected clients

👉 Requires monitor mode + wireless adapter

